# 5. OFFLINE-FIRST ARCHITECTURE

The application must continue working when the user has no Internet connection.

Offline users must be able to:

- View assigned projects
- View cached BOQ
- Create DPR
- Create measurements
- Create WIR
- Create MIR
- Create MAS
- Add site photographs
- Add snag
- Add manpower
- Update progress
- Create site observations
- Create tasks
- Save documents metadata

When Internet becomes available:

```text
Local Data
   ↓
Sync Queue
   ↓
API
   ↓
Google Sheets
   ↓
Sync Confirmation
   ↓
Local Record Updated
```

Implement:

- Sync Queue
- Retry mechanism
- Failed sync status
- Conflict detection
- Last Sync Time
- Manual Sync
- Automatic Sync
- Sync Logs

Use:

```text
Record_ID
Updated_At
Version
Updated_By
```

for conflict management.

